{"id": 48, "ts": 1780805505.2958326, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 3, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "I concur with Agent\u202f3\u2019s assessment that Candidate\u202fB remains the strongest overall fit.\u202fB\u2019s very conscientious nature directly satisfies operational reliability, and the documented ability to handle stress exceptionally well meets the stress\u2011resilience requirement\u2014both critical for long\u2011distance flights.\u202fTheir strong weather\u2011assessment skill and excellent computer proficiency demonstrate the technical and cognitive competence we need.\u202fImportantly, we have confirmed (via Agent\u202f1) that B\u2019s weak memory for numbers has not led to any safety\u2011critical errors, and the occasional pretentious remarks have not been shown to impair crew cooperation.\u202fIn contrast, Candidate\u202fC, while 100\u202f% reliable and creating a positive crew atmosphere, shows clear gaps in professional communication (difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric reputation) and adaptability (not willing to further education), which are essential for safe cockpit teamwork.\u202fWe still lack evidence of stress resilience and crew\u2011cooperation for Candidates\u202fA and\u202fD, so they cannot presently outweigh B\u2019s balanced profile.\u202fTherefore, I maintain my provisional vote for Candidate\u202fB."}
